 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Relative affine-line weight step",
 "statement": "For the projection $p:\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0}\\to Y_0$ and every\n$K\\in D_{\\le w}(\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0})$, one has\n$Rp_!K\\in D_{\\le w}(Y_0)$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.md",
  "place": "node thm-zl-relative-line-step, order 2848"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-complex-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Apply [lem-zl-sheaves-to-complexes]. It says that, for a separated finite-type map, the complex upper-weight assertion follows once every mixed Weil sheaf of weights at most $v$ has $R^a p_!$ mixed of weights at most $v+a$ for every $a$. Thus it is enough to prove this sheaf-level assertion for the relative affine-line projection $p$.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-sheaves-to-complexes",
    "def-weil-complex-weights"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof, opening reduction to the sheaf assertion"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "Let $\\mathcal F$ be mixed of weights at most $v$. By [def-weil-punctual-weights], it has a finite filtration by constructible Weil subsheaves whose successive quotients are punctually pure of weights at most $v$. The coefficient clause of [lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction] propagates a direct-image bound through every finite filtration, and the extension estimate [lem-a1-extension-bounds] is the stalkwise weight step used in the long exact sequences. It therefore suffices to prove the sheaf bound for one punctually pure graded piece.",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-punctual-weights",
    "lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction",
    "lem-a1-extension-bounds"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof, finite weight filtration and extension reduction"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "For a punctually pure graded piece, apply [thm-zl-relative-line-stratification]. It gives finite source and target stratifications on which the sheaf is lisse and each induced map is either separated quasi-finite or smooth with one-dimensional affine geometric fibers. On a smooth relative-curve stratum, [thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core] gives that $R^a p_!\\mathcal F$ is mixed of weights at most $v+a$; on a separated quasi-finite stratum, [lem-zl-quasi-finite] gives the same upper-weight bound. Restricting a punctually pure sheaf to a stratum preserves that purity by the definition in [def-weil-punctual-weights]. When a stratum map is viewed as a composite with its locally closed target immersion, [lem-zl-shriek-composition] identifies the resulting exceptional direct image with the corresponding stratumwise piece of $Rp_!$.",
   "uses": [
    "thm-zl-relative-line-stratification",
    "thm-zl-relative-affine-curve-core",
    "lem-zl-quasi-finite",
    "def-weil-punctual-weights",
    "lem-zl-shriek-composition"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof, stratified pure graded piece"
   }
  },
  {
   "text": "The finite source and target stratifications can be ordered as successive open--closed decompositions. Apply the source and target clauses of [lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction] inductively to reassemble the sheaf-level direct-image bounds from the stratumwise bounds. The corresponding localization triangles are glued at the complex level by [lem-zl-open-closed-weight]. Combining this reassembly with Step 1 yields $Rp_!K\\in D_{\\leq w}(Y_0)$ for every $K\\in D_{\\leq w}(\\mathbf A^1_{Y_0})$.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction",
    "lem-zl-open-closed-weight",
    "lem-zl-sheaves-to-complexes"
   ],
   "elementary": false,
   "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/thm-zl-relative-line-step.proof.md",
    "place": "Proof, open--closed reassembly"
   }
  }
 ],
